{"skill":{"slug":"meta-ads","displayName":"Meta Ads"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770005815556,"changelog":"Initial release of Meta Ads API skill.\n\n- Full read/write integration with Meta (Facebook) Ads API.\n- Manage ad accounts, campaigns, ad sets, ads, and ad creatives.\n- Access detailed performance insights and metrics for accounts and campaigns.\n- Provides clear setup instructions, required permissions, and authentication steps.\n- Includes ready-to-use API request examples for all major ad management actions.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"skill.md","size":15626,"sha256":"cde5fbb94b3f45a1eee08dd2d526612224afb3f0274739ca62e41e5d5ad9c80e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2076,"sha256":"85f1bc9aab7bf151c68fc8466506054f70ef805dc73076c123f63a094e42b901","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789027820467,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"b07d932df23ff58c8b9a0d97908865ad0950e25bab743d6ce520c79c4acb4b88","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/b07d932df23ff58c8b9a0d97908865ad0950e25bab743d6ce520c79c4acb4b88","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: meta-ads\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides a full read/write integration with the Meta Ads API. All `curl` commands in `skill.md` target the legitimate Meta Graph API endpoint (graph.facebook.com) and perform actions consistent with managing ad campaigns, ad sets, ads, and retrieving insights. The required environment variables (`META_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID`) and permissions (`ads_read`, `ads_management`) are explicitly stated and necessary for the skill's functionality. There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution patterns (e.g., `curl|bash`), persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts designed to subvert the agent's core function or access unrelated sensitive data.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160809170},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":53,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":10,"checkedAt":1789027820467},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This Meta Ads skill is coherent documentation for managing ads, but it encourages broad, long-lived Meta ad-management access and destructive operations without enough safeguards.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The documented environment requires a Meta access token and ad account ID, recommends ads_read plus ads_management, and later recommends an Admin system user token for production; that is broader and longer-lived than many read-only or limited management workflows need.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact is a Markdown skill reference only; I found no bundled executable code, install hook, dependency installer, or remote payload retrieval in the workspace artifacts.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill presents high-impact write and delete commands as normal examples without clear confirmation, approval, rollback, or safer-default guidance such as preferring pause or archive over delete.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill recommends system user tokens that do not expire and an Admin role, creating durable production authority without documented rotation, least-privilege scoping, or monitoring guidance.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is full read/write Meta Ads API management, and the examples match that purpose, but the capability includes financially consequential actions such as activating campaigns, changing budgets, and deleting campaigns, ad sets, and ads.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this skill carefully before installing. Use it only with a narrowly scoped Meta credential, avoid query-string tokens, keep tokens in a secret manager, separate read-only from management use, and require explicit human approval before activating, budget-changing, or deleting ad assets.","findings":"[PE3] expected: References to META_ACCESS_TOKEN are expected for a Meta Ads API reference and are not evidence of credential theft by themselves; the concern is weak security handling guidance around those credentials.\n[E1] expected: Calls to https://graph.facebook.com are expected for this integration and appear purpose-aligned, not hidden exfiltration.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The scanner concern about token handling is supported: the skill allows query-parameter tokens and recommends long-lived production tokens without enough least-privilege, storage, rotation, or leakage warnings.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The scanner concern about destructive operations is supported: delete examples for campaigns, ad sets, and ads lack explicit confirmation or business-impact warnings.\n[T09] unexpected: The SARIF concern is supported because the skill documents access tokens, app secrets, and token-debug values in URL query strings, which can leak via logs, history, and process listings.\n[T05] unexpected: The SARIF concern is supported because the skill recommends an Admin system user with ads_read and ads_management and notes that system user tokens do not expire.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789027820467}}}}}